-- title:
--   Unique place above each supersingular place of X₀(M')_κ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q \ge 5$ and a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and write $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Inside the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ consider $E_0 =$ `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$, the $\kappa$-subfield generated by the reduced $q$-expansions `jqModC` $\kappa$ and `jqNModC` $\kappa\,M'$, and $E =$ `xHFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, the $q$-expansion function field attached to the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ for $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Assume $E_0 \le E$ as intermediate fields and that the resulting inclusion $E_0 \hookrightarrow E$ is integral. Let $s$ be a place of $E_0$ over $\kappa$ (a proper valuation subring of $E_0$ containing $\kappa$ and being a principal ideal ring) which lies in `ssPlaces` $q\,M'\,\kappa$, i.e. $s$ is rational, satisfies `IsAffineGeomPlace` $\kappa\,M'$, and the value of $s$ at `jGeomGen` $\kappa\,M'$ lies in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet` $q\,\kappa$. Then there is exactly one place $w$ of $E$ over $\kappa$ whose restriction along the inclusion $E_0 \hookrightarrow E$ — the preimage in $E_0$ of the valuation subring of $w$ — equals $s$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Igusa covering of $X_0(M')$ in characteristic $q$ is totally ramified over the supersingular locus: each supersingular place of the reduced function field of $X_0(M')$ carries a single place of the reduced full-level field at $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$. It is used in the identification of valuation subrings and integral structures at supersingular places, in particular by the descent statements characterising places of the full-level field by their behaviour on the Igusa ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_existsUnique_place_restrictAlong_eq_of_mem_ssPlaces.lean

